## The Setting Math at 2.5ct — Three Honest Scenarios

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Stone</th><th>Setting Allocation</th><th>Total Ring</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Lab + platinum halo</strong></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30163288?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$3,289 2.82ct Ideal lab</a></td><td>$4,711 platinum pavé halo + V-tip prongs</td><td>$8,000</td><td>Our lab pick zone. Reads as $14k+ ring.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Natural + minimal setting (BAD)</strong></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29458684?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$34,151 H-VS1 Ideal natural</a></td><td>$1,849 basic 14k prong</td><td>$36,000</td><td>The $12,000 Setting Trap. Reads as $22k ring. Avoid.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Natural + proper platinum setting</strong></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29458684?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$34,151 H-VS1 Ideal natural</a></td><td>$12,000 platinum pavé halo + V-tip + accent diamonds</td><td>$46,151</td><td>Our natural pick zone. Reads as $55k+ ring.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Max natural + max setting</strong></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30188924?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">$49,918 2.5ct D-VS1 Ideal</a></td><td>$15,000+ platinum three-stone</td><td>$65,000+</td><td>Full-prestige natural tier.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** Three scenarios work at 2.5ct. The lab scenario at $8k is the smartest value play. The natural scenario at $46k is the honest natural buy. The natural scenario at $36k with a minimal setting is the trap to avoid — the stone is dressed down by the setting and loses $10k+ in perceived value.

> **"If a client comes in with $35,000 and wants natural 2.5ct, I tell them two things. One — the stone will cost $34k. Two — plan another $12k for the setting. Either they stretch to $46k total, or they step down to a 2ct natural at $28k and put the $7k saved into a $12k setting instead. Trying to do a $34k natural with a $1,500 setting is the trap."** — Farzana Hasan, GIA Diamond Expert

