## How to Verify a 2.5 Carat Marquise Before You Buy

Three checks every stone must pass before you add to cart.

**Check 1 — The certificate measurements.** For a 2.5ct marquise at 2.00 L:W, measurements should read close to 14.5 × 7.25 × 4.5 mm. If length is below 14.0 mm, the stone is cut deep and wasting carat weight below the girdle. More in our [marquise ideal proportions guide](/marquise-cut-diamond-ideal-proportions).

**Check 2 — The HD video for bow-tie severity.** Open the 360° HD video on the retailer listing. At 2.5ct the Bow-Tie Certainty is in play — the question is severity. Ideal cut keeps it faint. Reject stones with hard dark bands across the center of the table. See [marquise diamond bow-tie](/marquise-diamond-bow-tie).

**Check 3 — Confirm setting will use V-tip prongs or bezel.** The V-Tip Prong Mandate at 2.5ct is non-negotiable. Before you buy the stone, confirm the setting you want supports V-tip prongs or a protective bezel. Standard round prong settings fail this check.

I run these three checks on every 2.5ct marquise before I quote a client. The stone has to pass the first two. The setting choice is the third — and often the difference between a ring that lasts 50 years intact and a ring that comes back with a chipped tip after 18 months.

