Updated {{month_year}} with current certified market inventory — 6 natural GIA stones at 2.5–2.6ct and 20+ lab-grown stones at 2.5–2.9ct marquise. Natural inventory ranged from **$30,114 (sub-threshold)** to **$49,918**. Lab inventory floor is **$3,283** for the Lab Septet (seven identical IGI E-VVS2 stones at this price). Added the $12,000 Setting Trap framework after three clients at this tier walked in with budgets that priced only for the stone and skipped the setting entirely. Added the V-Tip Prong Mandate because I've seen 15 chipped marquise tips this year — all set in standard round prongs. Our picks remain the IGI 2.82ct E-VS1 Ideal lab at $3,289 and the GIA 2.5ct H-VS1 Ideal natural at $34,151.

